  "body": "## The problem\n\nThe Windows installer deferred whenever any launcher was running: it staged the wheel and a detached helper waited (up to 6h) for every launcher pid to exit before running `uv tool install --force`. The user explicitly wants the install to **complete immediately** even with `mcc-claude`/`fcc-claude` windows open — open windows keep old code, new sessions/servers get the new version.\n\n## Why deferring existed\n\nWindows refuses to **delete** a uv tool directory a process runs from (interpreter + loaded `.pyd` held open), so `uv tool install --force` fails partway. But Windows **allows renaming** a directory a process runs from, and a running process keeps already-loaded modules in memory. Verified live: a loaded `.pyd` and the entire tool dir can be renamed while a real session runs from it.\n\n## The fix\n\n`Install-FreeClaudeCode` now, when launchers are running:\n1. Renames the old tool env aside → `my-claude-code.old-<ts>`.\n2. Runs `uv tool install --force` into the fresh canonical path.\n3. Best-effort removes the `.old-*` dir (kept open by live windows → becomes orphaned garbage swept on next install).\n4. **Rename failure** (rare hard lock) → falls back to the previous detached-helper deferral.\n5. **Failed fresh install** → renames the old dir back, so the user is never left with no working tool.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New tests: rename-then-reinstall (stub uv recreates the fresh tool dir, old dir gone) + rollback-on-failed-install. Existing deferred-helper tests still pass (fallback retained).\n- Static: ruff format/check, ty clean. PS tests run on Windows CI.\n- **Live test pending post-merge**: run the published scriptblock URL with launchers open to confirm immediate completion (the URL serves `main`, so this lands after merge).\n\nVersion 5.3.1 → 5.3.2.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
