    "message": "fix(install): Windows update completes immediately even with launchers open\n\nThe Windows installer deferred whenever a launcher was running: it staged the\nwheel and a detached helper waited (up to 6h) for every launcher pid to exit\nbefore running `uv tool install --force`. The user wants the install to finish\nnow, with open windows unaffected and only new sessions/servers picking up the\nnew version.\n\nWindows refuses to DELETE a uv tool directory a process runs from (interpreter +\nloaded .pyd held open), but it ALLOWS RENAMING it, and a running process keeps\nits already-loaded modules in memory. So the installer now renames the old tool\nenv aside (`my-claude-code.old-<ts>`) and runs `uv tool install --force` into\nthe fresh canonical path: open windows keep running old code, new windows and\nrestarted servers get the new version -- matching POSIX semantics.\n\nRename failure (rare hard lock) falls back to the previous detached-helper\ndeferral; a failed fresh install renames the old dir back so the user is never\nleft with no working tool; stale .old-* dirs are swept best-effort on the next\ninstall. Verified live that a loaded .pyd and the whole tool dir can be renamed\nwhile a real session runs from it.\n\nTests: new rename-then-reinstall test (stub uv recreates the fresh tool dir)\nand rollback-on-failure test; existing deferred-helper tests still pass (the\nfallback remains). Version 5.3.1 -> 5.3.2.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
